<h3>Request overview — required characteristics of sending, and the responsibility boundary</h3>
<p>The sending stage calls for the following characteristics. (The choice of queue technology and the topology are left to the Platform team's judgement; the request assumes a Kafka base.)</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Asynchronous · surge absorption</strong> — separate the decision from the sending, and buffer momentary bursts of sends in the queue.</li>
  <li><strong>Delivery guarantee</strong> — send without loss, and confirm whether the message actually arrived.</li>
  <li><strong>Reprocessing</strong> — retry transient failures automatically; isolate repeated failures and reprocess them manually.</li>
  <li><strong>Accurate timing</strong> — send according to the timing type: immediate, delayed, recurring, transition.</li>
  <li><strong>Scalability</strong> — keep up as channels and volume grow.</li>
</ul>
